1. The miniKanren implementation of The Reasoned Schemer, first edition

   Files:   miniKanren/trs1/main.rkt

   Source:  Daniel P. Friedman, William E. Byrd, and Oleg Kiselyov,
            The Reasoned Schemer, MIT Press, 2005: chapter 9
            ("Under the Hood") and appendix A ("Connecting the Wires").
            The same code is also published at
            https://github.com/miniKanren/TheReasonedSchemer,
            which does not state a license.

   Copyright (C) 2005 Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

   miniKanren/trs1/main.rkt is a Typed Racket rewrite of that code.  The
   changes are: type definitions and annotations throughout; a single
   answer in a stream is represented by a one-element list and the empty
   stream by '(); streams are accessed through a few stream operations
   (stream-first, stream-rest, and so on), with which case∞ is defined
   and which replace mzero, unit, and choice; ext-s performs the occurs check (so == is the checked
   unification); and #s, #u, and the goal and thunk lambdas are spelled
   succeed, fail, λG, and λF.


