3. The miniKanren implementation of The Reasoned Schemer, second edition

   Files:   miniKanren/trs2/main.rkt
            miniKanren/trs2/tests/arith.rktl

   Source:  https://github.com/TheReasonedSchemer2ndEd/CodeFromTheReasonedSchemer2ndEd
            (trs2-impl.scm and trs2-arith.scm), the code of chapters
            7, 8, 10 and appendix A of
            Daniel P. Friedman, William E. Byrd, Oleg Kiselyov, and
            Jason Hemann, The Reasoned Schemer, second edition, MIT
            Press, 2018.

   miniKanren/trs2/main.rkt is a Typed Racket rewrite of that code.  The
   changes are: type definitions and annotations throughout (defrel
   gives an argument the type Term unless it is annotated, and the
   result the type Goal); variables are structs compared with eq? and
   named after the fresh identifier; literals are compared with equal?
   instead of eqv?; ext-s skips the occurs check for ground terms; and
   the stream functions reach streams only through a few operations
   (stream-first, stream-rest, stream-cons, and so on) that read a
   suspension as an element pause.
   miniKanren/trs2/tests/arith.rktl adapts the arithmetic code with a
   type annotation for build-num; the shared list helpers are provided
   by the chapter tests.  The code is distributed under the following
