5. microKanren

   Files:   microKanren/main.rkt
            microKanren/tests/programs.rktl, core.rktl, wrappers.rktl

   Source:  https://github.com/jasonhemann/microKanren
            (microKanren.scm, miniKanren-wrappers.scm,
            microKanren-test.scm, microKanren-test-programs.scm), from
            Jason Hemann and Daniel P. Friedman, "μKanren: A Minimal
            Functional Core for Relational Programming", Scheme
            Workshop 2013.

   microKanren/main.rkt is a Typed Racket rewrite of microKanren.scm
   and miniKanren-wrappers.scm.  The changes are: type definitions and
   annotations throughout; variables are structs holding their counter
   instead of vectors; literals are compared with equal? instead of
   eqv?; the stream functions reach streams only through a few
   operations (stream-first, stream-rest, stream-cons, and so on) that
   read a suspension as an element pause; and mzero, unit, pull, take,
   and take-all are replaced by empty-stream, stream, stream-force,
   stream-force-take, and stream->list.  The tests are adapted from the test files and from the test
   programs in miniKanren-wrappers.scm.  The code is distributed under
